    "['type [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 65410', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco command for the Juniper BGP configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65410\\nneighbor EBGP peer-group\\nneighbor EBGP ebgp-multihop 255\\nneighbor EBGP remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco equivalent requires establishing the BGP process first with the AS number (65410 from the Juniper config)\\n2. \"peer-group\" in Cisco serves a similar purpose to \"group\" in Juniper\\n3. \"ebgp-multihop\" is added since this is an external BGP configuration\\n4. The remote AS (100) matches the Juniper \"peer-as\" setting\\n5. The actual neighbor IPs would be configured separately in Cisco using this peer-group', 'trans_template': 'router bgp 65410'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor EBGP peer-group', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco command for the Juniper BGP configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65410\\nneighbor EBGP peer-group\\nneighbor EBGP ebgp-multihop 255\\nneighbor EBGP remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco equivalent requires establishing the BGP process first with the AS number (65410 from the Juniper config)\\n2. \"peer-group\" in Cisco serves a similar purpose to \"group\" in Juniper\\n3. \"ebgp-multihop\" is added since this is an external BGP configuration\\n4. The remote AS (100) matches the Juniper \"peer-as\" setting\\n5. The actual neighbor IPs would be configured separately in Cisco using this peer-group', 'trans_template': 'neighbor EBGP peer-group'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor EBGP ebgp-multihop 255', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [paramet