    "['peer-as [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 65410', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65410\\nneighbor 192.168.1.1 remote-as 100\\nneighbor 172.16.1.1 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Cisco configuration requires the local AS number (65410 from the Juniper config) to be specified in the 'router bgp' statement, while the peer AS (100) is specified in each neighbor statement. I've included both neighbor commands since they're part of the same BGP group in the original Juniper configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 65410'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 192.168.1.1 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65410\\nneighbor 192.168.1.1 remote-as 100\\nneighbor 172.16.1.1 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Cisco configuration requires the local AS number (65410 from the Juniper config) to be specified in the 'router bgp' statement, while the peer AS (100) is specified in each neighbor statement. I've included both neighbor commands since they're part of the same BGP group in the original Juniper configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 192.168.1.1 remote-as 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 172.16.1.1 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65410\\nneighbor 192.168.1.1 remote-as 100\\nneighbor 172.16.1.1 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Cisco configuration requires the local AS number (65410 from the Juniper config) to be specified in the 'router bgp' statement, while the peer AS (100) is specified in each neighbor statement. I've included both neighbor commands since they're part of the same BGP group in the original Juniper configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 172.16.1.1 remote-as 100'}]]": 1,
