    "['neighbor [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 172.16.1.1 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nneighbor 172.16.1.1 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command configures a BGP neighbor at 172.16.1.1 for the EBGP group\\n- In Cisco:\\n  - \"neighbor [IP] remote-as [AS]\" is the equivalent command\\n  - The AS number (100) comes from the \"peer-as 100\" statement in the Juniper configuration\\n  - Cisco doesn\\'t require separate group definitions like Juniper does\\n  - The EBGP type is implied by the AS number being different from the local AS (65410)', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 172.16.1.1 remote-as 100'}]]": 1,
